I like that idea, but it seems that it would be really hard to code. You
would have to do some good AI for strategy, or else it would give really
lousy, or stupid and obvious advice.

The hardest part would be to know when to have it shut up. Ideally, it would
only offer advice when it's a good idea that the player doesn't know about.
If it's simply a warning system that your hit points are low, or that you're
hungry, I would prefer something like flashing characters at the stats
screen instead of a shoulder imp.

And it would be really annoying to have these 'help' messages when I already
know what to do. Yes, I know my hit points are low, yes I know I have a
potion of healing, yes I am about to drink it! Shut up!

And, the imp should be called 'Clippy'.

